# Wheel and Ring - TMIL (the plan's TMILL: a NAME is five characters), a TEST course (SPEC.md 130.54): the
# BZDEV=1 build's alone, after the shipped courses (the Makefile's BZ_TESTCRS), on no pad, with no shipped
# demo.  "The wheel and the ring" (docs/plans/BOUNCE-BONANZA-SOAK.md, whose per-leg table is this course's
# map): it carries what bonanzawheel's and bonanzaring's MILL, TRIAL and BENCH legs need, on ONE route the
# autopilot rolls in 723 steps (13.1 s, no fall, one kick) -
#  - the TOP is MILL's cell for cell (A at 16, the house, both WINDMILLS on KEEP tubes - seeds 16 and the
#    derived 36 - B at 20, C at 18), so bonanzaphys's gate logs and every poke there carry over by name:
#    3-word rotor lanes, a contact rotor at the doorway, a transit, a tube exit;
#  - B's ramp down along +y onto W (12), which the route crosses along +x past three BUMPERS (2-word,
#    lighting posts): post (17, 16) kicked on the route; post (7, 13) on A CROSSES THE RING'S END on the CGA
#    (lines 192 - 208, card row 102) and post (20, 16) on W on the Hercules (lines 352 - 368, row 90) - a
#    card row's offset is (rb R + 2 x) mod 8192, absolute, so the spot is the world's (bbcourse.ring_cross);
#  - the ball's own 3- and 4-word boxes cross the ring's end ON THE ROUTE: the Hercules at (21, 15) on W
#    (box word 45, row 90), the CGA at (19, 20) on F (box word 30, row 204);
#  - a DROP from W's east end onto F (8): its bounces give the shadow a box of its own, and with the LIFT's
#    box beside them a frame of THREE boxes on both cards;
#  - the LIFT (18, 22), L 6: F its high dock, the low floor L (2) its low one, low in the picture (a lift's
#    track and a rotor never share a CGA window);
#  - the CANNON from F along -x over L onto G (4), the goal: scrolling up and left after the descent's down
#    and right; occluder records laid over the ball on the route (W, from about frame 326); two clocks;
#  - the QUIET PAD Q (0) and its post (33, 42), off the route and below everything: bonanzawheel's CORNER
#    leg's LIGHT diagonal step (SPEC.md 130.13.7 item 5) - the post's first row on the window's bottom edge,
#    the ball held still on Q's flat floor at its centre, and nothing else in the window that moves (its
#    top, line 562 on the CGA / 564 on the Hercules, is about 60 lines under the lift's lowest reach and
#    further from every rotor, clock and tube).  Post 6 shares its window with both rotors and the clock.
# width 64 with origin 272: the reach's footprints fill the picture's 512 px, left (G) and right (B, W's end).
course TMIL "Wheel and Ring"
test             # SPEC.md 130.54: a test course - no pad, no shipped demo, no target owed
music windmill   # SPEC.md 130.50.3: every course names its song
width 64
origin 272
ball rubber
uses rotor tube

floor rect  6  9 11 14  flat 16           # A, the start tier (MILL's)
wall  rect  6  5 12  9  flat 22           # the windmills' house
floor rect 12  5 15  9  flat 20           # B, east of the house (MILL's, a column narrower)
floor rect  3  5  6  9  flat 18           # C, west of it
floor rect 13  9 15 13  ramp y 9 13 20 12 # B's descent along +y
floor rect 12 13 23 17  flat 12           # W, the posts' strip
wall  tile 22 17        flat 13           # the drop's chute wall
floor rect 18 18 26 22  flat 8            # F, the drop's floor and the cannon's
floor rect 14 20 18 23  flat 2            # L, the low floor: the lift's low dock, under the cannon's flight
floor rect 14 18 16 20  flat 2
wall  tile 17 19        flat 8.5          # the cannon's body
floor tile 16 19        flat 8            # its mouth
floor rect 11 18 14 22  flat 4            # G, the goal ledge
goal  rect 11 18 13 21  flat 4
floor rect 29 28 34 33  flat 0            # Q, the corner leg's quiet pad: off the route, far below it
floor rect 32 41 35 44  flat 0            # ...and its post's pad

tube keep   9 9  12 6  via 9 6            # the route's windmill: A to B
prop windmill 9 9  seed 16
tube keep   7 9   5 7  via 7 7            # the other: A to C
prop windmill 7 9
prop bumper  7 13                         # crosses the ring's end on the CGA
prop bumper 20 16                         # crosses it on the Hercules
prop bumper 17 16                         # kicked on the route
tube drop  22 16  22 18  out +y  height 2 # W to F
tube launch 18 19  16 19  speed -288 0 480   # F over L to G
prop platform 18 22 6                     # the lift: F (8) high, L (2) low
prop bumper 33 42                         # the corner leg's post, alone at the bottom

start 9 12
way  9 12
way  9  9
way 12  6
way 13  7
way 14 13
way 14 14
way 21 14
way 22 16
way 22 18
way 18 19
way 16 19
way 12 19

clock  6 13                               # MILL's place: off the route, out of both doorways' 3 x 3
clock 11 21                               # the finish clock (SPEC.md 130.22.6), G's front-left
